# Normalize line endings.
#
# Why this file exists: with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) the
# working tree gets CRLF while the repo stores LF. Biome's formatter expects
# LF, so `bun run lint` reported errors on every file on Windows checkouts —
# effectively unusable, and it masked genuine lint findings underneath.
# The same mismatch made generated files churn on every cross-platform edit.
#
# `eol=lf` pins LF in the working tree on every platform. Git still stores LF
# either way; this only changes what lands on disk at checkout.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only script formats that genuinely require CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch, never diff as text. `text=auto` detects most of these
# on content, but being explicit avoids a misdetection corrupting a file.
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
*.icns      binary
*.mp3       binary
*.pub       binary
*.minisig   binary
*.wasm      binary
*.ttf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary

# Generated — collapse in reviews and suppress conflict noise. `linguist-*`
# drives GitHub's diff view; `-diff` keeps them out of local diffs too.
src/routeTree.gen.ts linguist-generated=true
bun.lock             linguist-generated=true -diff
